      en: "The Royal Ontario Museum (ROM) in Toronto, Ontario, is one of the largest museums of natural history and world culture in North America. Founded in 1914, it has a collection of over 13 million objects. The building comprises the historic 1914 wing and the modern Michael Lee-Chin Crystal, opened in 2007. Exhibits include dinosaur fossils, Chinese art, and a significant collection of Indigenous artifacts. The ROM is located on Bloor Street and is a major cultural hub in Toronto.",
